/2018/12/07/vail-resorts-inc-mtn-q1-2019-earnings-conference-c.aspx"},{"c":"MTN 2019 Q1","e":"mtn","d":"2018-12-07","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Shaun Kelley","x":"But you also gave some incremental color around the impact or the overall experience on a blended average price increase.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2018/12/07/vail-resorts-inc-mtn-q1-2019-earnings-conference-c.aspx"},{"c":"MTN 2019 Q2","e":"mtn","d":"2019-03-08","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Rob Katz","x":"Total effective ticket price decreased 7.8% in the second quarter compared to the prior year, primarily due to higher skier visitation by season pass holders and the impact of the new Military Epic Pass, partially offset by price increases in both our lift ticket and season pass products.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/03/08/vail-resorts-mtn-q2-2019-earnings-conference-call.aspx"},{"c":"MTN 2019 Q2","e":"mtn","d":"2019-03-08","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Rob Katz","x":"But then, obviously, we then build from there and have a pretty consistent price increase strategy so that initial conversion has some potentially immediate dilution.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/03/08/vail-resorts-mtn-q2-2019-earnings-conference-call.aspx"},{"c":"MTN 2019 Q2","e":"mtn","d":"2019-03-08","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Michael Barkin","x":"As noted in our January press release, we are lowering our guidance for fiscal 2019, primarily due to the disappointing results from destination visitation in the pre-holiday period and also due to shortfalls from expectations at Whistler Blackcomb and our Tahoe resorts.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/03/08/vail-resorts-mtn-q2-2019-earnings-conference-call.aspx"},{"c":"MTN 2019 Q3","e":"mtn","d":"2019-06-06","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Robert A. Katz","x":"…price, or ETP increased 1.8% in the third quarter compared to the prior year, primarily due to price increases in both our lift ticket and season pass products, partially offset by higher skier visitation by season pass holders, lower ETP from the acquired Triple Peaks and Stevens Pass Resort…","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/06/06/vail-resorts-inc-mtn-q3-2019-earnings-call-transcr.aspx"},{"c":"MTN 2019 Q4","e":"mtn","d":"2019-09-26","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Michael Z. Barkin","x":"Total effective ticket price or ETP decreased 3.4% compared to the prior year, primarily due to higher skier visitation by season pass holders, lower ETP from the acquired resorts and the new Military Epic Pass partially offset by price increases in both our lift ticket and season pass products.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/09/26/vail-resorts-inc-mtn-q4-2019-earnings-call-transcr.aspx"},{"c":"MTN 2020 Q1","e":"mtn","d":"2019-12-09","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Robert A. Katz","x":"…and obviously include whatever indicators we have on that certainly in the decision we make about reaffirming guidance, but at the same time, I would say we don't have perfect information as we said, we have different lodging indicators, but in some cases they don't represent the totality of by…","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/12/09/vail-resorts-inc-mtn-q1-2020-earnings-call-transcr.aspx"},{"c":"MTN 2020 Q1","e":"mtn","d":"2019-12-09","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Robert A. Katz","x":"…we feel good, but those are always going to be variable, so what I'd say is, yeah, we obviously have taken the experience from last year and incorporated that in our thinking as we put our reaffirmed guidance this year, but of course there is always going to be uncertainty no matter what.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/12/09/vail-resorts-inc-mtn-q1-2020-earnings-call-transcr.aspx"},{"c":"MTN 2020 Q2","e":"mtn","d":"2020-03-09","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Robert A. Katz","x":"Total effective ticket price decreased 0.5% in the second quarter compared to the prior year with price increases in both our lift ticket and season pass products, offset by the inclusion of results from Peak Resorts, which generates a lower effective ticket price.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/03/09/vail-resorts-inc-mtn-q2-2020-earnings-call-transcr.aspx"},{"c":"MTN 2020 Q3","e":"mtn","d":"2020-06-04","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Robert A. Katz","x":"And we have very intentionally delayed having any call to action around price increases, benefit reductions or credit expirations.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/06/05/vail-resorts-inc-mtn-q3-2020-earnings-call-transcr.aspx"},{"c":"MTN 2020 Q3","e":"mtn","d":"2020-06-04","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Robert A. Katz","x":"And again, I think that we -- I think to the extent that there is technology or other productivity opportunities to take, kind of back at the house, cost out of our business, I think we'll always look to do that.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/06/05/vail-resorts-inc-mtn-q3-2020-earnings-call-transcr.aspx"},{"c":"MTN 2020 Q4","e":"mtn","d":"2020-09-24","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Rob Katz","x":"…declined $167 million compared to the prior year, while resort reported EBITDA declined $43 million over the same time period, reflecting $124 million in net cost reductions, driven by a combination of reduced seasonal labor and expenses, as well as significant overhead cost-saving actions.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/09/25/vail-resorts-mtn-q4-2020-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"MTN 2020 Q4","e":"mtn","d":"2020-09-24","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Michael Barkin","x":"On the cost savings, there is a component within that cost savings, which is marketing.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/09/25/vail-resorts-mtn-q4-2020-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"MTN 2021 Q1","e":"mtn","d":"2020-12-10","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Rob Katz","x":"…the first quarter declined $132.1 million compared to the prior year, while resort reported EBITDA declined only $18.1 million over the same time period reflecting cost reductions driven by a combination of reduced seasonal labor and expenses as well as significant overhead cost saving actions.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/12/11/vail-resorts-mtn-q1-2021-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"MTN 2021 Q3","e":"mtn","d":"2021-06-07","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Rob Katz","x":"And this September, there'll be a price increase or there were spring pass sales, which gave you spring benefits, but probably for many people, not as significant as the credit that was there last year.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/06/08/vail-resorts-mtn-q3-2021-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"MTN 2021 Q3","e":"mtn","d":"2021-06-07","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Rob Katz","x":"And I think that even if sometimes we lean in and are a little bit more aggressive on price in some areas, we still try and keep, to my earlier comments, a more ratable, more consistent approach to price increases.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/06/08/vail-resorts-mtn-q3-2021-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"MTN 2021 Q4","e":"mtn","d":"2021-09-23","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Kirsten Lynch","x":"As you know, we have a long history of taking consistent price increases on our pass business.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/09/24/vail-resorts-mtn-q4-2021-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"MTN 2021 Q4","e":"mtn","d":"2021-09-23","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Kirsten Lynch","x":"The lever of taking price increases is certainly a lever that is absolutely still available for us going forward from this new baseline that we've created from this reset.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/09/24/vail-resorts-mtn-q4-2021-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"MTN 2021 Q4","e":"mtn","d":"2021-09-23","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Michael Barkin","x":"…to drive margin expansion in fiscal 2022 through continued cost discipline, including significant cost savings that are a continuation of our focus on operating as efficiently as possible coming out of COVID-19. Our liquidity position remains strong, and we are confident in the free cash flow…","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/09/24/vail-resorts-mtn-q4-2021-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"MTN 2021 Q4","e":"mtn","d":"2021-09-23","l":"cost_cuts","r":"analyst","s":"Laurent Vasilescu","x":"Maybe, Michael, I have a question here on G&A. I think you talked about cost-saving initiatives.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/09/24/vail-resorts-mtn-q4-2021-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"MTN 2022 Q2","e":"mtn","d":"2022-03-14","l":"cost_cuts","r":"analyst","s":"Shaun Kelley","x":"Just wondering, Kirsten, if you can help us dig in a little deeper on maybe some of the restructuring or initiatives that you're taking here?","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2022/03/14/vail-resorts-mtn-q2-2022-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"MTN 2022 Q3","e":"mtn","d":"2022-06-09","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Kirsten Lynch","x":"Pass sales dollars are benefiting from the 7.5% price increase relative to the 2021/2022 season, largely offset by the impact of the growth of Epic Day Pass products, including our new lower-priced Epic Day Pass offering.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2022/06/10/vail-resorts-mtn-q3-2022-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"MTN 2022 Q3","e":"mtn","d":"2022-06-09","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Kirsten Lynch","x":"We did take a price increase in Memorial Day.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2022/06/10/vail-resorts-mtn-q3-2022-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"MTN 2022 Q4","e":"mtn","d":"2022-09-28","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Kirsten Lynch","x":"Pass sales dollars continue to benefit from the 7.5% initial price increase and subsequent incremental price increases relative to the 2021-2022 season, largely offset by the mix impact of the growth of new pass holders into Epic Day Pass products, including our new lower-priced Epic Day Pass…","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2022/09/28/vail-resorts-mtn-q4-2022-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"MTN 2022 Q4","e":"mtn","d":"2022-09-28","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Kirsten Lynch","x":"…sales dollars continue to benefit from the 7.5% initial price increase and subsequent incremental price increases relative to the 2021-2022 season, largely offset by the mix impact of the growth of new pass holders into Epic Day Pass products, including our new lower-priced Epic Day Pass…","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2022/09/28/vail-resorts-mtn-q4-2022-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"MTN 2025 Q4","e":"mtn","d":"2025-09-29","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Angela Korch","x":"We anticipate growth in fiscal 2026 to be driven by price increases, ancillary capture, incremental efficiencies related to the resource efficiency transformation plan, and normalized weather conditions in Australia in 2026, partially offset by lower pass unit sales which are expected to have a…","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2025/09/29/vail-resorts-mtn-q4-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"MTN 2025 Q4","e":"mtn","d":"2025-09-29","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Rob Katz","x":"And so what I'd say is, you know, in a way, the big if we're cracking something open, it's not necessarily that we're looking to take price up or price down per se.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2025/09/29/vail-resorts-mtn-q4-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"MTN 2025 Q4","e":"mtn","d":"2025-09-29","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Rob Katz","x":"So while we do see that there'll be additional investments that we have to make, both within our marketing group and, of course, on the mountain, in our employees, as we, you know, look to take the experience of we also feel like there are other opportunities for us to take cost out of the business.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2025/09/29/vail-resorts-mtn-q4-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"MTN 2026 Q1","e":"mtn","d":"2025-12-10","l":"streaming","r":"analyst","s":"Rob Katz","x":"We have also shifted our marketing to better capture guests at the top of the funnel, a key to building awareness, and have expanded marketing in channels where younger consumers spend most of their time, including social, video, connected TV, and streaming audio.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2025/12/10/vail-resorts-mtn-q1-2026-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"MTN 2026 Q1","e":"mtn","d":"2025-12-10","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Angela Korch","x":"Expanding on our 2026 capital plan, we announced a core capital investment plan of $215 million to $220 million, which reflects the growth in inflation, including the impact from tariffs.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2025/12/10/vail-resorts-mtn-q1-2026-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"MTN 2026 Q1","e":"mtn","d":"2025-12-10","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Angela Korch","x":"Similar to last quarter, our guidance assumes growth from price increases and ancillary capture, as well as the assumed benefit from the approximately $38 million incremental efficiencies related to the resource efficiency transformation plan, offset partially by lower pass units, which are…","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2025/12/10/vail-resorts-mtn-q1-2026-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"MTN 2026 Q1","e":"mtn","d":"2025-12-10","l":"